{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:MassEndomorphism.ChiV21HoefsmitMatrixDerivation","@type":"LeanModule","name":"MassEndomorphism.ChiV21HoefsmitMatrixDerivation","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic"],"declarations":30,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.chi_v21_closed_form_u_coord","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.chi_v21_closed_form_u_coord","kind":"theorem","line":425,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-endomorphism/chi-v21-hoefsmit-matrix-derivation.lean#L425-L439","doc":"**Sqrt-free closed form** for V_(2,1) character difference,\nusing the polynomial b² = (q⁴ + q² + 1)/(q² + 1)² substitution.\n\nFor any abstract b_arg with `b_arg² = b_sq q`, the matrix-product\ntrace identity reduces to a rational equation in q alone — no\n`Real.sqrt` required. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.sigma1_v21_param_sq_trace","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.sigma1_v21_param_sq_trace","kind":"theorem","line":412,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-endomorphism/chi-v21-hoefsmit-matrix-derivation.lean#L412-L422","doc":"σ_1 squared: diagonal entries involve b_arg², off-diagonal\ninvolves b_arg·(d_1 + d_2). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.sigma1_v21_param","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.sigma1_v21_param","kind":"def","line":403,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-endomorphism/chi-v21-hoefsmit-matrix-derivation.lean#L403-L410","doc":"**Parameterised Hoefsmit σ_1**: off-diagonal coupling supplied\nas a free parameter `b_arg`, not constrained to `√(b²)`. The\ntrace of products with EVEN σ_1 count is polynomial in\n`b_arg²`, so the final formula doesn't need sqrt. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.chi_v21_matrix_trace_identity","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.chi_v21_matrix_trace_identity","kind":"theorem","line":296,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-endomorphism/chi-v21-hoefsmit-matrix-derivation.lean#L296-L387","doc":"**Full V_(2,1) Hoefsmit matrix-product trace identity.**\nThe trace of the matrix product on the canonical typed-B_3\nword for β_n minus β_p equals the closed form\n`-(q⁴+1)(q²-1) / (4q³)`.\n\nSubstantively verified via sympy's `q_character_on_braid_word`\n+ `sympy.cancel` + `sympy.factor` in the probe; the bit-exact\nclosed form recorded in `per-wedderburn-block-ck.witness.json`.\n\n**PROVED sorry-free 2026-09-04** (bean `qou-18b6`). Two things had to\nhappen, in this order, and the first was not what the file expected.\n\n**It was FALSE until the same day.** Until the `d_1`/`d_2` transposition\nwas fixed (see `hoefsmit_v21_d1`), these matrices gave\n\n    chi_n - chi_p = -(q-1)(q+1)(q⁴+1)(q²-q+1)(q²+q+1) / (4q⁵)\n\nwhich is the right-hand side below times `(q⁴+q²+1)/q²`. The note that\nstood here — \"the claim is exactly the one sympy verifies\" — was not true\nof *these definitions*, and no proof existed to be found. The closed form\nitself was never in doubt: at `q = 1+ε` it reproduces the ε-coefficients\nin `_deprecated/per-wedderburn-block-ck.witness.json` exactly, while the\ntransposed matrices do not.\n\n**The proof, and the two things that make it go through.** Expand with\n`simp only` over the definitions and `List.foldl_cons`, then\n`Matrix.mul_fin_two` folds the eleven factors into one `!![_,_;_,_]`.\nThen:\n\n* **Project with `Matrix.trace_fin_two_of`, not `Matrix.trace_fin_two`.**\n  The former rewrites `trace !![a,b;c,d]` straight to `a + d`; the latter\n  leaves `M 0 0 + M 1 1` as *applications*, which blocks everything after\n  it. This is the whole difference between a goal that closes and one\n  that does not, and it is invisible from the two lemma names.\n* **Only then generalise the square root.** `Real.sqrt (hoefsmit_v21_b_sq q)`\n  becomes a free `b` carrying `b² = (q⁴+q²+1)/(q²+1)²`; `ring_nf`\n  normalises, and `rw [hb4, hb2]` eliminates `b` entirely — `b⁴` first,\n  since `rw [hb2]` cannot see inside it. `field_simp; ring` finishes.\n\n**Why no `linear_combination` certificate is needed, contrary to the\nearlier note.** Only EVEN powers of `b` reach the trace: each index-1\nfactor is symmetric with off-diagonal `b`, so a path from a diagonal slot\nback to itself takes an even number of off-diagonal steps. Odd powers do\noccur — `b³` appears 20 times in the normalised matrix — but only in the\nOFF-diagonal entries, which the trace discards. Projecting first is what\nmakes the substitution `b² ↦ …` sufficient on its own.\n\n**Measured dead end, recorded so it is not re-walked.** With\n`Matrix.trace_fin_two` instead, the goal stays as index applications,\n`field_simp` runs on the un-projected expression and **exhausts\n2 000 000 heartbeats**. Per the trap this file already carries, the\nheartbeat bump was applied first, so that is a real exhaustion and not a\ndefault-budget timeout.\n\nThe statement is unchanged from when it carried the `sorry`; only the\nmatrices it is about were corrected. Bean `qou-18b6`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.chi_v21_on_word","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.chi_v21_on_word","kind":"def","line":285,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-endomorphism/chi-v21-hoefsmit-matrix-derivation.lean#L285-L289","doc":"The V_(2,1) character on a typed-B_3 word: trace of the\nmatrix product. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.crossing_to_matrix","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.crossing_to_matrix","kind":"def","line":272,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-endomorphism/chi-v21-hoefsmit-matrix-derivation.lean#L272-L283","doc":"Convert a typed crossing into its 2×2 matrix on V_(2,1).\nUsing the Hecke quadratic: σ_inv = σ - (q - q⁻¹) I,\naveraged = σ - (q - q⁻¹)/2 I. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.beta_n_word_v21","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.beta_n_word_v21","kind":"def","line":264,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-endomorphism/chi-v21-hoefsmit-matrix-derivation.lean#L264-L269","doc":"Canonical neutron typed-B_3 word (11 crossings, per\n`atom_canonical_crossings(Z=0, N=1)`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.beta_p_word_v21","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.beta_p_word_v21","kind":"def","line":257,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-endomorphism/chi-v21-hoefsmit-matrix-derivation.lean#L257-L262","doc":"Canonical proton typed-B_3 word (11 crossings, per\n`atom_canonical_crossings(Z=1, N=0)`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.TypedB3Word","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.TypedB3Word","kind":"def","line":253,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-endomorphism/chi-v21-hoefsmit-matrix-derivation.lean#L253-L255","doc":"A typed-B_3 word is a List of (generator index, crossing type)\npairs. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.TypedCrossingV21.avg","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.TypedCrossingV21.avg","kind":"ctor","line":251,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-endomorphism/chi-v21-hoefsmit-matrix-derivation.lean#L251-L251","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.TypedCrossingV21.siginv","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.TypedCrossingV21.siginv","kind":"ctor","line":250,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-endomorphism/chi-v21-hoefsmit-matrix-derivation.lean#L250-L250","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.TypedCrossingV21.sig","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.TypedCrossingV21.sig","kind":"ctor","line":249,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-endomorphism/chi-v21-hoefsmit-matrix-derivation.lean#L249-L249","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.TypedCrossingV21","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.TypedCrossingV21","kind":"inductive","line":247,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-endomorphism/chi-v21-hoefsmit-matrix-derivation.lean#L247-L251","doc":"Typed-crossing variant. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.hoefsmit_v21_braid_relation","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.hoefsmit_v21_braid_relation","kind":"theorem","line":221,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-endomorphism/chi-v21-hoefsmit-matrix-derivation.lean#L221-L245","doc":"**The braid relation `σ_0 σ_1 σ_0 = σ_1 σ_0 σ_1` on `V_(2,1)`** — stated\nfor the generic Tier-2 form with the off-diagonal `b` a free parameter\nconstrained only by `b² = d_1 d_2 + 1`.\n\nThis is the relation the file did not have, and its absence is what let a\ntransposed `(d_1, d_2)` stand: trace, determinant and the Hecke quadratic\nare each **symmetric** in `d_1, d_2`, so all three hold for the wrong\nmatrix. The braid relation couples `σ_0` and `σ_1`, and it is the\ncheapest statement that does. See `hoefsmit_v21_d1`.\n\nNote it needs no hypothesis on `b` beyond the quadratic — in particular\nno `0 ≤ b²` and no square root — so it holds over any field, which is\nthe Tier-2 point. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.sigma1_v21","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.sigma1_v21","kind":"def","line":214,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-endomorphism/chi-v21-hoefsmit-matrix-derivation.lean#L214-L218","doc":"Backward-compatibility alias — `sigma1_v21` is the legacy form.\nPhase 2 migrates this file's downstream uses to `sigma1_v21_gen`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.sigma1_v21_legacy","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.sigma1_v21_legacy","kind":"def","line":205,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-endomorphism/chi-v21-hoefsmit-matrix-derivation.lean#L205-L212","doc":"**Legacy archimedean form** of `sigma1_v21` — instantiates the\noff-diagonal as `Real.sqrt (hoefsmit_v21_b_sq q)` without an explicit\n`0 ≤ hoefsmit_v21_b_sq q` hypothesis. Use `sigma1_v21_gen` in new\ncode with an explicit square-root witness. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.sigma1_v21_gen","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.sigma1_v21_gen","kind":"def","line":196,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-endomorphism/chi-v21-hoefsmit-matrix-derivation.lean#L196-L202","doc":"The Hoefsmit σ_1 matrix on V_(2,1) — **Tier 2 generic-R form**.\nThe off-diagonal entry `b` is taken as an abstract square-root of\n`hoefsmit_v21_b_sq q`; downstream consumers supply the witness either\nformally (`u² = q` style adjoin) or archimedeanly. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.sigma0_v21","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.sigma0_v21","kind":"def","line":192,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-endomorphism/chi-v21-hoefsmit-matrix-derivation.lean#L192-L194","doc":"The Hoefsmit σ_0 matrix on V_(2,1): `diag(q, -q⁻¹)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.chi_V21_difference_at_two","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.chi_V21_difference_at_two","kind":"theorem","line":178,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-endomorphism/chi-v21-hoefsmit-matrix-derivation.lean#L178-L182","doc":"At q = 2 (ε = 1): closed form = -(17)(3)/(4·8) = -51/32. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.chi_V21_difference_at_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.chi_V21_difference_at_one","kind":"theorem","line":172,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-endomorphism/chi-v21-hoefsmit-matrix-derivation.lean#L172-L176","doc":"At q = 1: vanishes (isospin invariance). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.chi_V21_laurent_decomposition","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.chi_V21_laurent_decomposition","kind":"theorem","line":162,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-endomorphism/chi-v21-hoefsmit-matrix-derivation.lean#L162-L168","doc":"The Laurent decomposition of the V_(2,1) closed form:\n`(−q⁶ + q⁴ − q² + 1)/(4q³) = -q³/4 + q/4 - q⁻¹/4 + q⁻³/4`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.chi_V21_difference_factored_eq_polynomial","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.chi_V21_difference_factored_eq_polynomial","kind":"theorem","line":145,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-endomorphism/chi-v21-hoefsmit-matrix-derivation.lean#L145-L150","doc":"**Factored ↔ polynomial form** identity. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.chi_V21_difference_polynomial","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.chi_V21_difference_polynomial","kind":"def","line":138,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-endomorphism/chi-v21-hoefsmit-matrix-derivation.lean#L138-L140","doc":"V_(2,1) polynomial form: `(-q⁶ + q⁴ - q² + 1) / (4q³)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.chi_V21_difference_factored","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.chi_V21_difference_factored","kind":"def","line":129,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-endomorphism/chi-v21-hoefsmit-matrix-derivation.lean#L129-L136","doc":"**V_(2,1) closed form** (factored): `-(q⁴+1)(q²-1) / (4q³)`.\n\nDUPLICATION TRACKING: also defined as `chi_V21_diff_closed`\nin `rem:chi-per-irrep-cyclotomic-closed-forms`. Local copy\nhere for self-containment; centralisation deferred per the\nchapter-block file-isolation convention. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.hoefsmit_v21_sigma1_trace","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.hoefsmit_v21_sigma1_trace","kind":"theorem","line":112,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-endomorphism/chi-v21-hoefsmit-matrix-derivation.lean#L112-L118","doc":"σ_1 trace identity: d_1 + d_2 = q - q⁻¹. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.hoefsmit_v21_sigma0_trace","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.hoefsmit_v21_sigma0_trace","kind":"theorem","line":108,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-endomorphism/chi-v21-hoefsmit-matrix-derivation.lean#L108-L110","doc":"σ_0 trace = q - q⁻¹ (diagonal with entries q and -q⁻¹). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.hoefsmit_v21_b_sq_rational","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.hoefsmit_v21_b_sq_rational","kind":"theorem","line":85,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-endomorphism/chi-v21-hoefsmit-matrix-derivation.lean#L85-L98","doc":"The b² expression as a rational function of q (= polynomial in\nu = q² over (u + 1)²).\n\n**Moved up from the end of the file.** `chi_v21_matrix_trace_identity`\nbelow consumes it, and Lean is order-sensitive: declared after its\nconsumer, it produced `Unknown identifier hoefsmit_v21_b_sq_rational`\nat the use site — a forward reference, not a missing declaration, and\nthe two are indistinguishable from the error text alone. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.hoefsmit_v21_b_sq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.hoefsmit_v21_b_sq","kind":"def","line":80,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-endomorphism/chi-v21-hoefsmit-matrix-derivation.lean#L80-L83","doc":"The Hoefsmit off-diagonal coupling squared:\n`b² = d_1 · d_2 + 1 = (q⁴ + q² + 1) / (q² + 1)²`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.hoefsmit_v21_d2","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.hoefsmit_v21_d2","kind":"def","line":75,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-endomorphism/chi-v21-hoefsmit-matrix-derivation.lean#L75-L78","doc":"The Hoefsmit `d_2` diagonal entry — the `(1,1)` entry of `σ_1`:\n`q³ / (q² + 1)`. See `hoefsmit_v21_d1` for why this is not the other\nway round. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.hoefsmit_v21_d1","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.hoefsmit_v21_d1","kind":"def","line":50,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-endomorphism/chi-v21-hoefsmit-matrix-derivation.lean#L50-L73","doc":"The Hoefsmit `d_1` diagonal entry — the `(0,0)` entry of `σ_1`:\n`-q⁻¹ / (q² + 1)`.\n\n**CORRECTED 2026-09-04 (bean `qou-18b6`): `d_1` and `d_2` were\ntransposed.** They read `d_1 = q³/(q²+1)`, `d_2 = -q⁻¹/(q²+1)`, which\nwith this file's `σ_0 = diag(q, -q⁻¹)` does **not** satisfy the braid\nrelation `σ_0 σ_1 σ_0 = σ_1 σ_0 σ_1` — so the pair was not a\nrepresentation of `B_3` at all, and every trace computed from it was\nof something that does not exist.\n\nNothing in the file could detect it, and that is the point: `b² =\nd_1·d_2 + 1`, `d_1 + d_2 = q - q⁻¹` and `det = -1` are all **symmetric\nin `d_1, d_2`**, so `hoefsmit_v21_b_sq_rational`, `hoefsmit_v21_sigma1_trace`\nand the Hecke quadratic hold verbatim under the transposition. Only a\nrelation involving `σ_0` and `σ_1` *together* separates them, which is\nwhy `hoefsmit_v21_braid_relation` below is now stated.\n\nTwo independent confirmations of the corrected assignment: solving\n`{trace = q - q⁻¹, det = -1, braid}` for `(d_1, d_2, b)` returns this\none (up to the sign of `b`, and the degenerate `b = 0`); and at `q = 1`\nit gives `σ_1 = !![-1/2, √3/2; √3/2, 1/2]`, the classical Young\northogonal form of `s_2` on the 2-dimensional representation of `S_3`.\nThe transposed version gave `+1/2` in the `(0,0)` slot. ","signatureChunk":0}]}